## [:< ##

# name  = plugin.user-edit.example.tab_info
# descr = minimal reference plugin's self-description
# param = -none-

## THROWAWAY / reference only -- see plugin.user-edit.example.init_code's own
## note.
##
## REAL BUG, found live and fixed : this originally pinned 'location' -- a
## REAL default field on every actual record [ users.record.default_fields ]
## -- to make live testing easy.  plugin.user-edit.example stayed wired into
## plugins.load afterward [ per user, "keep it and clean it up later" ], so
## that pin was ACTIVE against every real user's real record too, not just
## test ones : 'location' silently became readonly, two-stage-Right-to-enter,
## test-plugin-append-only-edited for EVERYONE, the moment phase_2 shipped.
## pinned_keys must NEVER name a key from users.record.default_fields /
## .optional_fields while this plugin stays wired for live smoke-testing --
## 'example_test_field' [ below ] cannot collide with anything real, and a
## throwaway test record can still carry it directly via users.value-set
## [ schema_from_record derives fields from whatever a record actually has,
## not a fixed list, so an arbitrary extra key works fine for this ].
return {
    qw| label |       => qw| example |,
    qw| pinned_keys | => [qw| example_test_field |],
};

